---
import { cardCls } from '../lib/ui';
// The ship's sieves, now the one home for sieves (9 November: the top-level Sieves tab moved here). How hard
// each layer is pushed, how far it moves, where it changes regime, which way it steers, and when it settles.
---
<div class="shiptab" id="sieves">
  <h1>Sieves <span class="q">how the ship answers the wind, layer by layer: how hard each layer is pushed, how far it moves, and which way it steers</span></h1>
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
    <p class="lede">The <b>wind</b> is the error on each guess: how far the bet was from the word that came, felt by every weight that took part. A <b>tack</b> is the ship's answer, one training update: its direction from the wind, its size from the learning rate. <b>Trim</b> is how the tack is set. The three sieves read every layer's tacks, every 50 steps; a <b>kink</b> (◆) is the step where a layer changes regime, the break of a two-line fit, firm after <span id="kinkrule"></span>.</p>
  </section>
  <div class="cards" id="sievecards"></div>
  <div class="row">
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Gradient push per layer <span class="note">log10 of the pre-clip norm; ◆ the kink</span></h2><div class="chart" id="gradheat"></div></section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Weight move per layer <span class="note">log10 of the move since the last record over the size of the weights; ◆ the kink</span></h2><div class="chart" id="moveheat"></div></section>
  </div>
  <div class="row">
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>The kink <span class="note">each layer's push, fitted as two lines; the break is where the layer changes regime</span></h2>
      <div class="chart" id="kinks"></div>
    </section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>Where each layer broke</h2>
      <div class="scroll"><table class="kinks" id="kinktable"><thead><tr>
        <th>layer</th><th>kink at step</th><th>which way</th><th>slope before</th><th>slope after</th><th>strength</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
      <div class="foot" id="kinknote"></div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Heading <span class="note">the cosine between each layer's last two moves: 1 holds its angle, 0 wanders, below 0 comes about</span></h2><div class="chart" id="sieve-heading"></div></section>
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
    <h2>Settled <span class="note">for each layer, the first step its heading stays at 0.8 or more for three records running, beside the step any star lit in that layer; do headings settle from the bottom up, and does a layer settle when its star lights?</span></h2>
    <div class="scroll"><table id="settledtable"><thead><tr><th>layer</th><th>heading settled at</th><th>heading now</th><th>push kink</th><th>stars lit in this layer</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
  </section>
</div>
